---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const skills = {
  "Languages": ["Java", "TypeScript", "JavaScript", "Golang", "Python"],
  "Frameworks": ["React", "Node.js", "Astro", "FastAPI"],
  "Tools": ["Git", "Docker", "PostgreSQL", "Linux"],
};
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Vincent Nguyen — Software Engineer">

  <!-- Header -->
  <section class="pb-7 border-b border-slate-100">
    <p class="text-blue-600 font-semibold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">About Me</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900">
      Hey again, I'm Vince 👋
    </h1>
  </section>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-1 gap-16 py-8 border-b border-slate-100">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-5">Why software engineering?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Coding since 2021. Problem-solving since 2008. Cold since 2003. 🥶
        </p>
        <p>
          I’d be lying if I said I always knew I wanted to be a software engineer. Honestly, software engineering wasn’t even on my radar until the week before I had to lock in my degree.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whether it was Mathematics and Chemistry in high school, Data Structures and Algorithms at UNSW, or shipping real features at Atlassian, the feeling has always been the same — going to bed completely stuck, then waking up with a path forward. Ignore the hours of tossing and turning in between.
        </p>
        <p>
          So software engineering? More of a means than an end. And the end isn’t early retirement — those dreams might be cooked anyway. The end is simpler than that: a career that still feels rewarding on Monday morning. Most Mondays at least.
        </p>
        <p>
          The latest challenge? AI.
        </p>
        <p>
        And honestly, I love it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I feel lucky to have entered the industry right as AI started reshaping it. Even then, it somehow still feels impossible to keep up. Every week there’s a new tool, a new optimisation, a new breakthrough — and at this point I’ve genuinely lost count.
        </p>
        <p>
          Half the time I’m excited. The other half I’m wondering whether the next grad is about to put me out of a job.
        </p>
        <p>
          So consider this little website proof that the cycle continues: learning, building, problem-solving, improving. That’s always been the part I enjoy most anyway 😊
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-5">What else besides software engineering?</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          When I'm not delivering shareholder value, you'll find me
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
            <li>kickboxing and gymming (I look like I've not stepped 50 metres within a gym in my life)</li>
            <li>rewatching how i met your mother (the children yearn for the yearn)</li> 
            <li>at my local Oporto (single-handedly funding expansion plans)</li>
            <li>teaching Chemistry at Peak HSC (shoutout to the one student who liked my classes enough to leave a google review)</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


  </div>

  <!-- Contact -->
  <section class="pt-14">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Get in Touch</h2>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-5">

      <a href="https://github.com/CSVince" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="GitHub" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">
        <!-- GitHub -->
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M12 0C5.374 0 0 5.373 0 12c0 5.302 3.438 9.8 8.207 11.387.599.111.793-.261.793-.577v-2.234c-3.338.726-4.033-1.416-4.033-1.416-.546-1.387-1.333-1.756-1.333-1.756-1.089-.745.083-.729.083-.729 1.205.084 1.839 1.237 1.839 1.237 1.07 1.834 2.807 1.304 3.492.997.107-.775.418-1.305.762-1.604-2.665-.305-5.467-1.334-5.467-5.931 0-1.311.469-2.381 1.236-3.221-.124-.303-.535-1.524.117-3.176 0 0 1.008-.322 3.301 1.23A11.509 11.509 0 0 1 12 5.803c1.02.005 2.047.138 3.006.404 2.291-1.552 3.297-1.23 3.297-1.23.653 1.653.242 2.874.118 3.176.77.84 1.235 1.911 1.235 3.221 0 4.609-2.807 5.624-5.479 5.921.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222v3.293c0 .319.192.694.801.576C20.566 21.797 24 17.3 24 12c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12z"/>
        </svg>
      </a>

      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vincent-nguyen-539906183/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="LinkedIn" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-blue-600 transition-colors">
        <!-- LinkedIn -->
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433a2.062 2.062 0 0 1-2.063-2.065 2.064 2.064 0 1 1 2.063 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/>
        </svg>
      </a>

      <a href="mailto:vvvincent288@gmail.com" aria-label="Email" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-blue-600 transition-colors">
        <!-- Mail -->
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="16" rx="2"/>
          <path d="m22 7-8.97 5.7a1.94 1.94 0 0 1-2.06 0L2 7"/>
